   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in relation\nto promotions of detectives",
    "basePrintNo": "S5659",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5659-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §14-114, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5659\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the administrative code of the city of\nNew York, in relation to promotions of detectives\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends the administrative code of the city of New\nYork to allow for the promotion of detectives in the third or second\ngrades who have a certain number of years of service.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that this act shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill gives detectives with fifteen (15) years of service in the 3rd\ngrade and detectives with (10) years of service in the 2nd grade an\nincentive to stay with the New York City Police Department by allowing\nthem to retire at their respective grades and receive pension and\nprevents the loss of valuable experience and knowledge of proven and\neffective police tactics to retirement.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n2018: S6098B - committed to Rules\n2017: S6098A - committed to Cities\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
